# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Layers Superfood Bar website — what is NOT version-controlled.
# The repo holds everything needed to rebuild and edit the site: page sources,
# content files, the photo originals that are placed on the site, album photos
# and the tooling. Business papers and the raw media archive stay out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Business papers (agreement, proposal, client notes) — never in the repo
contract/
deliverable/
Layers-Services-Agreement*
Layers-Website-Proposal.md
DELIVERABLE.md
*.pdf

# Design history and the client's old prototypes (reference only)
design/
reference/

# Raw media archive: unplaced photos and the film's source clips.
# The finished film is committed under public/assets/video/.
src-img/library/
src-video/clips/
src-video/*.mp4

# Instagram feed photos: downloaded by every build from Behold (tools/instagram.py)
src-img/instagram/

# Build reports (written by every tools/build.py run; CI posts the .md)
build-report.json
build-report.md

# Local tooling state
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log

# The GitHub Pages copy tools/ci/prefix.py writes when run in the repo root
_site/
